WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.946
HR-driven identity is an organizational
change before it's a technical one,

2
00:00:04.946 --> 00:00:08.025
and most of the owners sit
outside the CIO's shop.

3
00:00:08.025 --> 00:00:10.237
The rule is one decider per row.

4
00:00:10.237 --> 00:00:14.694
The governance body settles who owns
each attribute and the person key,

5
00:00:14.694 --> 00:00:17.413
because those bind
several offices at once.

6
00:00:17.413 --> 00:00:19.951
HR owns the meaning of its own codes.

7
00:00:19.951 --> 00:00:25.687
Security owns leaver timing, and the
authorizing official accepts any residual risk.

8
00:00:25.687 --> 00:00:29.832
The failures on the right share one
root: in a ticket-driven estate,

9
00:00:29.832 --> 00:00:32.901
whoever can make a change
ends up owning the data.

10
00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:35.925
Privacy arriving at
go-live is the costliest.

11
00:00:35.925 --> 00:00:37.250
Next, the plan.
